# Tests that fail in the toolbox container and pass on CI.
#
# `scripts/ci` reports these and does not fail on them; anything else fails the run. A
# name here is a claim that has been checked against a green CI run, not a way to quieten
# something inconvenient — and a line that stops being true is a line to delete, which
# `scripts/ci` says out loud when one of these passes.
#
# One name per line, exactly as ExUnit prints it after the number.

# Spawns a real daemon in a real OS process and waits for it to answer on a unix socket.
# The generated launcher used to be unparseable here because the working tree was CRLF
# (`.gitattributes` fixes that); with LF it launches, writes its pidfile and creates the
# socket, and the client still does not get an answer inside the timeout. Unexplained,
# and green on CI: runs 35135673938 and 35137121967 both pass all 82 gateway tests.
ten concurrent clients spawn exactly one daemon
a stale lock left by a killed client does not block start-up forever
kill -9 with three sessions: all come back, the mid-turn one interrupted
an idle session stops its tree, and subscribing serves history without starting one

# Verifies a cancelled shell command's grandchild is gone by its OS pid. The container's
# process tree is not the runner's, and this has failed here since long before the
# packages that touch sessions.
cancel kills a shell command and its grandchild, verified by OS pid
